**A certain number of animals** participate in the Great Migration annually.

In a typical year, the Great Migration herds begin in **a certain area**. 
The Great Migration involves animals moving through Tanzania’s Serengeti National Park and Kenya’s Masai Mara National Reserve.

Around two million wildebeests, zebras, and Thomson’s gazelles participate in the Great Migration annually.

In a typical year, the Great Migration herds begin in the south of the Serengeti.

